        {
          "category": "Lair Action",
          "name": "Lair Actions",
          "description": "When fighting inside its lair, the dragon can invoke ambient magic on initiative count 20 (losing initiative ties) to take one of the following lair actions:\n• Grasping roots and vines erupt in a 20-foot radius centered on a point on the ground within 120 feet. That area becomes difficult terrain, and each creature there must succeed on a DC 15 Strength saving throw or be restrained.\n• A wall of tangled brush bristling with thorns springs into existence on a solid surface within 120 feet (up to 60 ft. long, 10 ft. high, 5 ft. thick). Creatures in its area must make a DC 15 Dexterity saving throw or take 18 (4d8) piercing damage.\n• Magical fog billows around one creature within 120 feet. The creature must succeed on a DC 15 Wisdom saving throw or be charmed by the dragon until initiative count 20 on the next round."
        },
